                "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
                "senderName": "NWS Corpus Christi TX",
                "headline": "Flash Flood Warning issued November 8 at 1:23PM CST until November 8 at 4:30PM CST by NWS Corpus Christi TX",
                "description": "FFWCRP\n\nThe National Weather Service in Corpus Christi has issued a\n\n* Flash Flood Warning for...\nSoutheastern Duval County in south central Texas...\nSouthwestern Jim Wells County in south central Texas...\nWestern Kleberg County in south central Texas...\n\n* Until 430 PM CST.\n\n* At 123 PM CST, local law enforcement reported flash flooding on\nHighways 141 and also 281 in Kleberg county. Between 5 and 8 inches\nof rain have fallen. Flooding impacts will continue, but no\nadditional rainfall is occurring. Flash flooding is already\noccurring.\n\nHAZARD...Flash flooding caused by heavy rain.\n\nSOURCE...Law enforcement reported.\n\nIMPACT...Flash flooding of small creeks and streams, urban areas,\nhighways, streets and underpasses as well as other poor\ndrainage and low-lying areas.\n\n* Some locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nKingsville, Premont, Ricardo, Kingsville Naval Air Station,\nRiviera, La Gloria and Loyola Beach.\n\nThis includes the following highways...\nUS Highway 281 between mile markers 688 and 706. US Highway 77\nbetween mile markers 690 and 708.\n\nThis includes the following streams and drainages...\nEbanito Creek, Derramadero de Machos, Paisano Creek, San Fernando\nCreek, Lagunas Negras, Jaboncillos Creek, Ramada del Toro Creek,\nTranquitas Creek, Baffin Bay, Salado Creek, Chiltipin Creek, Las\nAnimas Creek, Araa Creek, Escondido Creek, Cibolo Creek and Olmos\nCreek, Los.",
                "instruction": "Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.\n\nBe aware of your surroundings and do not drive on flooded roads.",
                "response": "Avoid",
                "note": null,
                "parameters": {
                    "AWIPSidentifier": [
                        "FFWCRP"
                    ],
                    "WMOidentifier": [
